{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #18 ADDENDUM 2 — board state + both epics' AC verification is DONE ===\n\nFOUR CHANGES IN FLIGHT, all rebased onto current main, all awaiting `Verified`:\n  1276  2b16 inbound link removal (LLM-Review +1 already)\n  1279  5200: pin the three repaired J11 oracles          } one stack; submitting the TIP (1283)\n  1280  5200: make three J11 live cells able to fail       } submits its ancestors\n  1283  5200: row-12-OUTBOUND cell (new)                   }\n88d9 is certified + claimed and BLOCKED only on 1276 landing (both touch `inbound_differ.py`, which sits\nat 797/800 — see #18 for the seam already chosen: `inbound_fields.py`).\n\n**BOTH epics' acceptance criteria have now been INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED, and the results are on the tickets\n— read them before ticking anything.**\n * e369's 13 ACs: **11 MET, 1 BLOCKED (AC1, the three open children), 1 AMENDED (AC5).** Full evidence in\n   the epic's AC-verification comment, including the run that proves the operator-attested bidirectional\n   criterion in ONE pass: **run 30718360110, job 91417809065, main @ 96b82de1e0, 26 passed / 0 skipped.**\n   AC5 was amended because its original wording demanded \"exactly one implementation reachable by both\n   backends\" for the rich-text codec and the user-identity model — an outcome that would be WRONG if\n   achieved (ADF vs wiki; `accountId` vs `name`). Two implementations of one pinned contract is correct.\n   The amendment also narrows the enforcement clause to what the checker actually does (it forbids\n   cross-IMPORTS; it cannot prevent a re-DEFINITION).\n * 5200's 18 ACs: verified earlier this session; criterion 11's three gaps are now closed or recorded\n   (row 1 outbound BUILT, row 12 outbound BUILT as 1283, row 14 inbound's oracle provably unsatisfiable\n   and amended).\n\n**A STANDING CAVEAT TO CARRY: \"the DC harness is green\" is NOT currently true.** The AC4 proving run was\n26/26 at main `96b82de1e0`; the latest recorded run (30772461871, main `bd3de0f864`) is 48 passed / 1\nfailed, and the suite has grown 49 → 58 cells, so **nine cells have never executed against the harness.**\nA fresh run is required before 5200 closes. Three of its cells are EXPECTED RED until 2b16/88d9 land —\nDO NOT invert them.\n\n**DECISIONS ON THE RECORD THIS STRETCH (do not silently re-decide any of them):**\n * OPERATOR: 5200's row-12-outbound gap is to be BUILT, not amended away. Done (1283).\n * OPERATOR: `e39f` (inbound link removal never converges for a two-relation pair) is a follow-up and does\n   NOT gate e369 — it fails safe.\n * MINE, and flagged BORDERLINE on its own ticket: `39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b` — **outbound parent-set can NEVER\n   be emitted for DC**, because the emit gate omits the parent unless the parent is an `epic`\n   (`outbound_field_diff._resolve_local_parent:136-139`, bug 8b25's hierarchy guard) while DC's\n   `set_parent` only accepts a SUB-TASK child (`jira_datacenter/transport.py:693-694`), whose parent is a\n   standard issue importing as `task`. Disjoint. FIFTH instance of \"Cloud has the translation, DC never got\n   its half\". Filed as NOT gating, consistent with the e39f ruling — but unlike e39f it does NOT fail safe,\n   it is a silent divergence, so the operator may prefer the strict reading. Reparenting is one command.\n\nFOLLOW-UPS FILED THIS SESSION, none gating: 275e · 59b2 · e39f · 6c0a · 39c1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785730794518382001,"uuid":"2c9ed0db-f648-4df3-94dd-15257b881f73"}